  "description": "ZONBIR crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H122 Gd9 O42 1+,6(H2 O1),H1 O1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd9 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.628-5.176 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.51-169.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd9(acac)16(μ3-OH)8(μ4-OH)2]OH·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
